		TO RUN COMPUTER

(I)	SET UP EQUIPMENT. IN THE SUBJECT ROOM CHECK:
CABLE FROM SENSORS PLUGGED INTO CONTROL BOX.
SUBJECT'S SWITCHES AND PUSH BUTTONS CONNECTED TO 18 PIN JONES PLUG.
EXTENSION SCOPE TURNED ON, AND BRIGHTNESS ALL THE WAY UP(CLOCKWISE)
CHANNELS 1+2 BOTH SELECTED.

IN COMPUTER ROOM:
APPROPRIATE MAC PANEL INSTALLED (______)
EXTENSION SCOPE PLUGGED IN TO APPROPRIATE ROOM.
ANALOG CABLES PLUGGED INTO CORRECT SOCKETS.

INTERFACE POWER TURNED ON.
COMPUTER POWER ON. (DO NOT LOCK)

(II)	DEADSTART OS/8:

MOUNT SYSTEM TAPE (_______) ON UNIT 0.

MOUNT DATA TAPE (_________) ON UNIT 1.

*TAPE MOUNTING:
*
*	PUT THE 3-POSITION (REMOTE-OFF-LOCAL) SWITCH IN LOCAL MODE.
*	THIS ENABLES THE TWO SWITCHES LABELED WITH ARROWS TO CONTROL THE TAPE.
*
*	IF THE WRONG TAPE IN ON THE DRIVE, PUSH THE RIGHT-HAND ARROW
*	TO WIND THE TAPE ONTO ITS REEL.
*	WHEN THE TAPE COMES OFF THE LEFT REEL, PUT THE SWITCH IN 'OFF' POSITION
*	STOP THE TAPE, AND PULL IT OFF.
*
*	WITH THE SWITCH IN 'OFF' POSITION, PUSH THE CORRECT REEL ONTO THE 
*	RIGHT-HAND HUB (PRESS IT ON FIRMLY)
*	WIND A FEW TURNS OF THE TAPE ONTO THE LEFT REEL BY HAND
*	THEN PUT THE SWITCH BACK INTO 'LOCAL' AND WIND MORE TAPE 
*	WITH THE LEFT-ARROW. KEEP WINDING FOR 5 TO 10 SECONDS.
*	RELEASE THE ARROW AND PUT THE SWITCH IN 'REMOTE' POSITION.
*	NOW THE COMPUTER CAN READ THE TAPE.
*
*	THE TAPES SHOULD GENERALLY BE LEFT 'WRITE-ENABLED'
*

	WHEN THE TAPES ARE MOUNTED:
PUSH ALL SWITCHES BACK EXECPT THE THREE LABELED 'DEADSTART'.
PUSH GREEN 'I/O PRESET' BUTTON.
PUSH YELLOW 'DO' BUTTON. UNIT 0 SHOULD SPIN BRIEFLY.
PUSH GREEN 'START-20' BUTTON. UNIT 0 WILL SPIN SOME MORE.
WHEN THE TAPE STOPS, A '.' WILL PRINT ON THE TELETYPE 
INDICATING THAT OS/8 IS READY. 
(IF '.' DOES NOT PRINT, PUSH 'RUBOUT' UNTIL IT DOES.)
ENTER THE CURRENT DATE; TYPE: 'DATE DD-MMM-YY' (EG: 14-DEC-78)


(III)	IN RESPONSE TO THE '.', TYPE: 'R ______'.
THE TAPE ON UNIT 0 WILL SPIN A BIT AND THE YOUR PROGRAM WILL START RUNNING.



(IV)	WHEN A '*' IS PRINTED ON THE TELETYPE YOU SHOULD TYPE IN 
THE APPROPRIATE OUTPUT AND INPUT FILE NAMES.
THE FORMAT FOR THE FILE NAMES IS:

	DEV:OUTPUT.EX<DEV:INPUT.EX

	DEV: IS THE DEVICE WHICH WILL HOLD THE FILE. THE CHOICES ARE:
	SYS: TAPE UNIT 0
	DSK: TAPE UNIT 1 (USUALLY THE DEFAULT)
	LPT: LINE PRINTER

	'OUTPUT' AND 'INPUT' ARE FILE NAMES OF SIX OR FEWER CHARACTERS.
	'.EX' IS AN OPTIONAL FILENAME EXTENSION
	AND WILL USUALLY BE '.DA' (OR '.__')

WHILE TYPING IN THE FILE NAMES, THE FOLLOWING KEYS WILL HELP YOU CORRECT ERRORS.

	^U: DELETE LINE AND TRY AGAIN
	RUBOUT: DELETE PRECEEDING CHARACTER
	LINE FEED: COMPUTER RETYPES CURRENT LINE.





(V)	USEFULL SYSTEM COMMANDS:

TO GET NAMES OF FILES ON TAPE:
USE:	.UA	LIST FILES ON UNIT 1
	.UB	LIST FILES ON UNIT 0

TO LIST CONTENTS OF A FILE:
	.LIST DEV:NAME.EX-L

TO RENAME A FILE:
	.REN NEW<OLD

TO DELETE A FILE FROM THE TAPE:
	.DEL DEV:NAME.EX

